ure — Human Soldier"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Triton Shorestalker","oracle_id":"71a60247-17e5-44bd-9fed-f7d550b09ef3","oracle_text":"This creature can't be blocked.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-04-19","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Merfolk Rogue"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"An attacking unblocked creature exists from the time the defending player chooses not to block that creature until the combat phase ends. Curtain of Light doesn’t have any legal targets outside of the combat phase.","oracle_id":"d6efbbf9-1449-45ce-b187-30041eb36d93","published_at":"2005-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Curtain of Light does trigger bushido abilities.","oracle_id":"d6efbbf9-1449-45ce-b187-30041eb36d93","published_at":"2005-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Curtain of Light isn’t particularly effective against creatures with trample. Since the creature with trample has no blocker to assign damage to, all the damage will be assigned to the defending player.","oracle_id":"d6efbbf9-1449-45ce-b187-30041eb36d93","published_at":"2005-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a turn has multiple combat phases, this spell can be cast during any of them as long as it’s after the beginning of that phase’s Declare Blockers Step.","oracle_id":"d6efbbf9-1449-45ce-b187-30041eb36d93","published_at":"2013-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Is not very useful against Trample creatures since Trample damage comes through as if a zero toughness creature blocked the Trampler.","oracle_id":"de96ef93-a2e0-409d-9d25-fcb2405039b5","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Works on creatures that can’t be blocked and on creatures that have special blocking requirements.","oracle_id":"de96ef93-a2e0-409d-9d25-fcb2405039b5","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the ability is used on a creature with Trample, the damage still comes through.","oracle_id":"730fbd6a-096c-4d25-9372-c05f90088f83","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This ability will trigger any creature’s “whenever this becomes blocked” ability.","oracle_id":"730fbd6a-096c-4d25-9372-c05f90088f83","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a turn has multiple combat phases, the ability can be activated during any of them as long as it’s after the beginning of that phase’s Declare Blockers Step.","oracle_id":"730fbd6a-096c-4d25-9372-c05f90088f83","published_at":"2013-09-20","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
